{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"GraphGeneration","kind":"identifier"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every structural mutation (an insertion, a removal, re-pointing an edge) starts a new"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"generation. Reserving capacity and writing attached map values do not. A structure derived from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a graph stores the graph’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"generation"},{"type":"text","text":" and calls "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isCurrent(for:)"},{"type":"text","text":" before it relies on the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"graph again."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A copy of a graph has the same generation as the original until either is mutated. Views and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"adaptors (a transposed view, an undirected view, a wrapper such as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedAcyclicGraph"},{"text":")","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"report their base’s generation, so a view and its base, though they may describe different","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"graphs, have equal generations. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isCurrent(for:)"},{"text":" answers only whether the storage of the graph","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"passed in is in the state the generation was read from; it does not tell which view the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"generation was read through. An untracked generation, from a representation that does not track","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"generations or a mutable graph never mutated, is current for no graph. Equal tracked","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"generations are the same structural state of the same storage, and every untracked generation","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"equals every other.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"topicSections":[{"title":"Instance Methods","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/GraphGeneration\/isCurrent(for:)-1rsfw","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/GraphGeneration\/isCurrent(for:)-1t817","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/GraphGeneration\/isCurrent(for:)-3zt2o","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/GraphGeneration\/isCurrent(for:)-5kltt","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/GraphGeneration\/isCurrent(for:)-scjl"],"anchor":"Instance-Methods"},{"title":"Type Properties","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/GraphGeneration\/untracked"],"anchor":"Type-Properties"},{"title":"Default Implementations","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/GraphGeneration\/Equatable-Implementations"],"anchor":"Default-Implementations"}],"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Conforms To","type":"conformsTo","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/s15BitwiseCopyableP","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/SQ","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"kind":"relationships"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/graphgeneration"]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/GraphGeneration"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"A graph’s generation: which structural state of which